        23
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.cityofleonard.net/page/About%20Leonard",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "A post office and school opened in 1860, marking the first civic institutions in Leonard.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        24
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.cityofleonard.net/page/About%20Leonard",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The town’s first newspaper, the Leonard Graphic, began in 1890 and is still in publication today.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        26
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.cityofleonard.net/page/About%20Leonard",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Leonard Collegiate Institute opened in 1894, moved into a three‑story building in 1906, and closed in 1914.",
